<%- ; Drop-in on the distro's docker.service. Attached to docker rather
   ; than to the stack's units because there are TWO paths that start
   ; containers -- systemd's <svc>.service units, and dockerd's own
   ; `restart: unless-stopped` policy at daemon start. Gating the stack
   ; units would leave the second path unguarded.
   ;
   ; Wants=, never Requires=: a failed or timed-out gate must not be
   ; able to keep docker down. Worst case is a ~60s delayed boot with
   ; the pre-existing race still present, which is strictly better than
   ; a host that boots with no containers.
   ;
   ; Only containers using docker's embedded resolver are affected by
   ; the race this closes. use_vpn services share wireguard's netns and
   ; its resolv.conf (one inode, bind-mounted from wireguard's
   ; container dir) and resolve through the tunnel at 10.128.0.1, so
   ; they never consult MagicDNS.
-%>
[Unit]
Wants=tailscale-dns-ready.service
After=tailscale-dns-ready.service
